/-!
# A self-centralizing elementary abelian subgroup of order sixteen in `Spin(7)`

Write `e₀, …, e₆` for the coordinate generators of the Clifford algebra of the negative-definite
form `realCliffordForm 0 7` on `ℝ⁷`, so that `eᵢ² = -1` and `eᵢ eⱼ = -eⱼ eᵢ` for `i ≠ j`. The
three fourfold products

`e₀e₁e₂e₃`, `e₀e₁e₄e₅`, `e₀e₂e₄e₆`

are the basis monomials `e_s` of the supports `s = {0, 1, 2, 3}`, `{0, 1, 4, 5}`, `{0, 2, 4, 6}`
(`CliffordAlgebra.basis_eq_prod_map_sort`). They have even degree and their generators have norm
`-1`, so they are elements of the Spin group (`CliffordAlgebra.basis_mem_spinGroup`). Their
supports pairwise meet in two indices, so they commute, and each squares to `1`. The supports are
independent over `𝔽₂`: together with `∅` the symmetric differences they generate are the eight
supports of `TauCeti.spinSevenSupports`. With the independent central sign `-1`, they therefore
generate an elementary abelian `2`-group `TauCeti.realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian` of order
`16`, consisting of the sixteen signed monomials `±e_s` for those eight supports
(`TauCeti.mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_iff`).

The subgroup is its own centralizer (`TauCeti.centralizer_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian`).
An element `x` of the Spin group commuting with it acts on `ℝ⁷` commuting with the three sign
changes by which `e₀e₁e₂e₃`, `e₀e₁e₄e₅` and `e₀e₂e₄e₆` act
(`CliffordAlgebra.spinVectorAction_basis_of_coe_eq`). Their joint eigenspaces are the seven
coordinate lines, since the seven indices lie in pairwise different combinations of the three
supports. So `x` acts by a diagonal sign change, of determinant one, which is the action of the
basis monomial `e_t` of an even support `t`; as the kernel of the action is `±1`, `x = ±e_t`.
Finally `e_t` commutes with the generators only when `t` is one of the eight supports.

The isomorphism `CliffordAlgebra.realCliffordSpinGroupEquivNeg 0 7` between the Spin groups of
the negative- and positive-definite forms transports the subgroup to the compact Spin group
`realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0`, as `TauCeti.realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian`, which is again its own
centralizer. Hence it is a maximal commutative subgroup of `Spin(7)`
(`TauCeti.eq_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_of_le`), and a finite one, although `Spin(7)` is
compact, connected and simply connected. In particular the subgroup lies in no torus. Every point
of a torus `∀ i, AddCircle (p i)` is twice another, so the image of a homomorphism from a torus
that contained the subgroup would be a commutative subgroup equal to it in which every element is
a square, hence trivial (`TauCeti.not_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_le_range`). This holds for
tori of every rank, and for homomorphisms that are not injective. The statement for a torus of
`Spin(7)` in the sense of `TauCeti.Lie.IsTorus`, a compact connected commutative subgroup, is
`TauCeti.not_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_le_of_isTorus`, proved from the vector representation
in `TauCeti.Topology.Algebra.CliffordAlgebra.Spin.Real.Seven`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.spinSevenSupports`: the eight supports `∅` and `{0, 1, 2, 3}`, `{0, 1, 4, 5}`,
  `{0, 2, 4, 6}` together with their symmetric differences.
* `TauCeti.IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven`: the property of a Spin element of `realCliffordForm 0 7`
  of being a signed basis monomial `±e_s`.
* `TauCeti.realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian`: the subgroup of the Spin group of
  `realCliffordForm 0 7` generated by `-1` and the three fourfold products.
* `TauCeti.realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian`: its image in the compact Spin group
  `realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_iff`: the elements are exactly the signed basis
  monomials `±e_s` with `s ∈ spinSevenSupports`.
* `TauCeti.isSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven_iff`: `IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g s` holds exactly when
  `g = e_s` or `g = -e_s`.
* `TauCeti.IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.mul`, `TauCeti.IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.mul_self` and
  `TauCeti.IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.eq_or_eq_negOne_mul`: the product of `±e_s` and `±e_t` is
  `±e_{s ∆ t}`, `±e_s` squares to `1` for `s ∈ spinSevenSupports`, and two signed basis monomials
  of the same support agree up to `-1`.
* `TauCeti.exists_isSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven_mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian`: for every
  `s ∈ spinSevenSupports`, the subgroup contains a signed basis monomial `±e_s`.
* `TauCeti.mul_self_eq_one_of_mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian`,
  `TauCeti.realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_isMulCommutative`,
  `TauCeti.natCard_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian`: it is an elementary abelian `2`-group of
  order `16`; `TauCeti.exponent_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian` records its exponent `2`.
* `TauCeti.centralizer_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian`,
  `TauCeti.centralizer_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian`: it is its own centralizer.
* `TauCeti.eq_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_of_le`: its image in the compact Spin group is a
  maximal commutative subgroup.
* `TauCeti.not_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_le_range`: its image in the compact Spin group lies
  in the image of no homomorphism from a torus.

## References

* R. L. Griess, Jr., *Elementary abelian p-subgroups of algebraic groups*, Geometriae Dedicata 39
  (1991), 253–305, for nontoral elementary abelian `2`-subgroups of Spin groups.
* H. B. Lawson and M.-L. Michelsohn, *Spin Geometry* (1989), Chapter I, §1–§2.
-/

public section

open scoped symmDiff

open Function

open CliffordAlgebra

namespace TauCeti

/-! ### The supports -/

/-- The eight supports of the elementary abelian subgroup: `∅`, the three supports
`{0, 1, 2, 3}`, `{0, 1, 4, 5}` and `{0, 2, 4, 6}`, and their symmetric differences
`{2, 3, 4, 5}`, `{1, 3, 4, 6}`, `{1, 2, 5, 6}` and `{0, 3, 5, 6}`. -/
def spinSevenSupports : Finset (Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) :=
  {∅, {0, 1, 2, 3}, {0, 1, 4, 5}, {0, 2, 4, 6}, {2, 3, 4, 5}, {1, 3, 4, 6}, {1, 2, 5, 6},
    {0, 3, 5, 6}}

/-- The defining list of the eight supports. -/
theorem spinSevenSupports_def : spinSevenSupports =
    {∅, {0, 1, 2, 3}, {0, 1, 4, 5}, {0, 2, 4, 6}, {2, 3, 4, 5}, {1, 3, 4, 6}, {1, 2, 5, 6},
      {0, 3, 5, 6}} :=
  (rfl)

/-- Membership in the eight supports. -/
theorem mem_spinSevenSupports {s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))} :
    s ∈ spinSevenSupports ↔ s = ∅ ∨ s = {0, 1, 2, 3} ∨ s = {0, 1, 4, 5} ∨ s = {0, 2, 4, 6} ∨
      s = {2, 3, 4, 5} ∨ s = {1, 3, 4, 6} ∨ s = {1, 2, 5, 6} ∨ s = {0, 3, 5, 6} := by
  simp only [spinSevenSupports_def, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton]

/-- The supports are closed under symmetric difference. -/
theorem symmDiff_mem_spinSevenSupports {s t : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))} (hs : s ∈ spinSevenSupports)
    (ht : t ∈ spinSevenSupports) : s ∆ t ∈ spinSevenSupports := by
  revert s t
  decide +kernel

/-- There are eight supports: the three generating supports are independent over `𝔽₂`. -/
@[simp]
theorem card_spinSevenSupports : spinSevenSupports.card = 8 := by
  decide +kernel

/-- Every support has even cardinality. -/
theorem even_card_of_mem_spinSevenSupports {s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))}
    (hs : s ∈ spinSevenSupports) : Even s.card := by
  revert s
  decide +kernel

/-- The sign of `e_s * e_s` in `CliffordAlgebra.basis_mul_basis`, together with the sign
`(-1) ^ #s` of the squares of the generators, is `+1` for every support. -/
private theorem square_parity : ∀ s ∈ spinSevenSupports,
    (∑ i ∈ s, (s.filter (· < i)).card + s.card) % 2 = 0 := by
  decide +kernel

/-! ### Signed basis monomials -/

/-- The Spin element `e_s` of an even support `s`. -/
private noncomputable def spinBasis (s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) (hs : Even s.card) :
    realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7 :=
  ⟨basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s,
    basis_mem_spinGroup (isOrthoᵢ_associated_realCliffordForm 0 7) hs <| by
      simp_rw [Pi.basisFun_apply, realCliffordForm_single_one_of_le (Nat.zero_le _),
        Finset.prod_const, hs.neg_one_pow]⟩

/-- The Spin element `e_s` is the basis monomial `e_s` of the Clifford algebra. -/
@[simp]
private theorem coe_spinBasis (s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) (hs : Even s.card) :
    (spinBasis s hs : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7)) =
      basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s :=
  rfl

/-- The central element `-1` of the Spin group of `realCliffordForm 0 7`. -/
private noncomputable def spinNegOne : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7 :=
  spinGroup.negOne _ (nondegenerate_realCliffordForm 0 7).ne_zero

/-- The property of a Spin element of `realCliffordForm 0 7` of being the signed basis monomial
`±e_s`. -/
def IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven (g : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7) (s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) :
    Prop :=
  (g : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7)) =
      basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s ∨
    (g : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7)) =
      -basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s

/-- A Spin element is a signed basis monomial `±e_s` exactly when it equals `e_s` or `-e_s`. -/
theorem isSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven_iff {g : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7}
    {s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))} :
    IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g s ↔
      (g : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7)) =
          basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s ∨
        (g : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7)) =
          -basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The product of `±e_s` and `±e_t` is `±e_{s ∆ t}`. -/
theorem IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.mul {g h : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7}
    {s t : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))} (hg : IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g s)
    (hh : IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven h t) : IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven (g * h) (s ∆ t) := by
  unfold IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven at *
  rw [Submonoid.coe_mul]
  exact mul_eq_or_of_eq_basis_or (isOrthoᵢ_associated_realCliffordForm 0 7)
    (fun i ↦ Or.inr <| by
      rw [Pi.basisFun_apply, realCliffordForm_single_one_of_le (Nat.zero_le _)]) hg hh

/-- A signed basis monomial `±e_s` with `s` a support squares to `1`. -/
theorem IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.mul_self {g : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7}
    {s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))} (hg : IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g s) (hs : s ∈ spinSevenSupports) :
    g * g = 1 := by
  have hss : basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s *
      basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s = 1 := by
    simp_rw [basis_mul_basis (isOrthoᵢ_associated_realCliffordForm 0 7), symmDiff_self,
      Finset.bot_eq_empty, basis_empty, Finset.inter_self, Pi.basisFun_apply,
      realCliffordForm_single_one_of_le (Nat.zero_le _), Finset.prod_const]
    rw [← pow_add, neg_one_pow_eq_pow_mod_two, square_parity s hs, pow_zero, one_smul]
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  rw [Submonoid.coe_mul, OneMemClass.coe_one]
  rcases hg with hg | hg <;> simp only [hg, neg_mul_neg, hss]

/-- Two Spin elements that are signed basis monomials of the same support agree up to `-1`. -/
theorem IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.eq_or_eq_negOne_mul {g h : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7}
    {s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))} (hg : IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g s)
    (hh : IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven h s) :
    g = h ∨ g = spinGroup.negOne _ (nondegenerate_realCliffordForm 0 7).ne_zero * h := by
  unfold IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven at hg hh
  simp only [Subtype.ext_iff, Submonoid.coe_mul, spinGroup.coe_negOne, neg_one_mul]
  rcases hg with hg | hg <;> rcases hh with hh | hh <;> simp [hg, hh]

/-! ### The elementary abelian subgroup -/

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup of order `16` of `Spin(7)`**, in the Spin group of the
negative-definite form `realCliffordForm 0 7`: the subgroup generated by `-1` and the three
fourfold products `e₀e₁e₂e₃`, `e₀e₁e₄e₅` and `e₀e₂e₄e₆` of coordinate generators. -/
noncomputable def realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian : Subgroup (realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7) :=
  Subgroup.closure {spinNegOne, spinBasis {0, 1, 2, 3} (by decide),
    spinBasis {0, 1, 4, 5} (by decide), spinBasis {0, 2, 4, 6} (by decide)}

/-- Every generator of the subgroup is a signed basis monomial with support in
`spinSevenSupports`. -/
private theorem exists_isSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven_of_mem_generators {g : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7}
    (hg : g ∈ ({spinNegOne, spinBasis {0, 1, 2, 3} (by decide),
      spinBasis {0, 1, 4, 5} (by decide), spinBasis {0, 2, 4, 6} (by decide)} :
        Set (realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7))) :
    ∃ s ∈ spinSevenSupports, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g s := by
  rcases hg with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
  · exact ⟨∅, by decide, Or.inr (by simp [spinNegOne])⟩
  all_goals exact ⟨_, by decide, Or.inl rfl⟩

/-- For every support `s ∈ spinSevenSupports`, the subgroup contains a signed basis monomial
`±e_s`. -/
theorem exists_isSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven_mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian
    {s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))} (hs : s ∈ spinSevenSupports) :
    ∃ g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g s := by
  -- The supports reached by products of generators contain the generating supports and are
  -- closed under symmetric difference.
  have h₀ : ∃ g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g ∅ :=
    ⟨1, one_mem _, Or.inl (by simp)⟩
  have hmul {t u : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))}
      (ht : ∃ g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g t)
      (hu : ∃ g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g u) :
      ∃ g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g (t ∆ u) := by
    obtain ⟨g, hg, hgt⟩ := ht
    obtain ⟨h, hh, hhu⟩ := hu
    exact ⟨g * h, mul_mem hg hh, hgt.mul hhu⟩
  have hA : ∃ g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g {0, 1, 2, 3} :=
    ⟨spinBasis {0, 1, 2, 3} (by decide), Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp), Or.inl rfl⟩
  have hB : ∃ g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g {0, 1, 4, 5} :=
    ⟨spinBasis {0, 1, 4, 5} (by decide), Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp), Or.inl rfl⟩
  have hC : ∃ g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven g {0, 2, 4, 6} :=
    ⟨spinBasis {0, 2, 4, 6} (by decide), Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp), Or.inl rfl⟩
  rw [mem_spinSevenSupports] at hs
  rcases hs with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
  · exact h₀
  · exact hA
  · exact hB
  · exact hC
  · have h : ({0, 1, 2, 3} : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) ∆ {0, 1, 4, 5} = {2, 3, 4, 5} := by decide
    rw [← h]
    exact hmul hA hB
  · have h : ({0, 1, 2, 3} : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) ∆ {0, 2, 4, 6} = {1, 3, 4, 6} := by decide
    rw [← h]
    exact hmul hA hC
  · have h : ({0, 1, 4, 5} : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) ∆ {0, 2, 4, 6} = {1, 2, 5, 6} := by decide
    rw [← h]
    exact hmul hB hC
  · have h : ({0, 1, 2, 3} : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) ∆ {0, 1, 4, 5} ∆ {0, 2, 4, 6} =
        {0, 3, 5, 6} := by
      decide
    rw [← h]
    exact hmul (hmul hA hB) hC

/-- **The elements of the elementary abelian subgroup are the signed basis monomials** `±e_s`,
for the eight supports `s ∈ spinSevenSupports`. -/
theorem mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_iff {g : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7} :
    g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian ↔ ∃ s ∈ spinSevenSupports,
      (g : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7)) =
          basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s ∨
        (g : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7)) =
          -basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s := by
  refine ⟨fun hg ↦ ?_, fun ⟨s, hs, hgs⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
  · induction hg using Subgroup.closure_induction with
    | mem g hg => exact exists_isSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven_of_mem_generators hg
    | one => exact ⟨∅, by decide, Or.inl (by simp)⟩
    | mul g h _ _ hg hh =>
      obtain ⟨s, hs, hgs⟩ := hg
      obtain ⟨t, ht, hht⟩ := hh
      exact ⟨s ∆ t, symmDiff_mem_spinSevenSupports hs ht, IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.mul hgs hht⟩
    | inv g _ hg =>
      obtain ⟨s, hs, hgs⟩ := hg
      rw [inv_eq_of_mul_eq_one_right (IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.mul_self hgs hs)]
      exact ⟨s, hs, hgs⟩
  · obtain ⟨h, hh, hhs⟩ :=
      exists_isSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven_mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian hs
    rcases IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.eq_or_eq_negOne_mul hgs hhs with rfl | rfl
    · exact hh
    · exact mul_mem (Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp [spinNegOne])) hh

/-- The central element `-1` lies in the elementary abelian subgroup. -/
theorem negOne_mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian :
    spinGroup.negOne _ (nondegenerate_realCliffordForm 0 7).ne_zero ∈
      realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian :=
  Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp [spinNegOne])

/-- **Every element of the elementary abelian subgroup squares to `1`.** -/
theorem mul_self_eq_one_of_mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian {g : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7}
    (hg : g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian) : g * g = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hgs⟩ := mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_iff.mp hg
  exact IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven.mul_self hgs hs

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup has order `16`**: its elements are the signed basis
monomials `±e_s` for the eight supports, and these are distinct. -/
@[simp]
theorem natCard_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian :
    Nat.card realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian = 16 := by
  have hb := isOrthoᵢ_associated_realCliffordForm 0 7
  have hQ (i : Fin (0 + 7)) : realCliffordForm 0 7 (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7)) i) = 1 ∨
      realCliffordForm 0 7 (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7)) i) = -1 :=
    Or.inr <| by rw [Pi.basisFun_apply, realCliffordForm_single_one_of_le (Nat.zero_le _)]
  -- The signed monomial `u • e_s` of a support `s` and a sign `u`.
  let F : spinSevenSupports × ℤˣ → realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7 := fun p ↦
    (if p.2 = 1 then 1 else spinNegOne) * spinBasis p.1 (even_card_of_mem_spinSevenSupports
        p.1.property)
  have hF (p : spinSevenSupports × ℤˣ) :
      ((F p : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7) : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7)) =
        ((p.2 : ℤ) • basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) p.1) := by
    rcases Int.units_eq_one_or p.2 with h | h <;> simp [F, h, spinBasis, spinNegOne]
  let f : spinSevenSupports × ℤˣ → realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian := fun p ↦
    ⟨F p, mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_iff.mpr ⟨p.1, p.1.property, by
      rcases Int.units_eq_one_or p.2 with h | h <;> simp [hF, h]⟩⟩
  have hbij : Bijective f := by
    refine ⟨fun p q hpq ↦ ?_, fun g ↦ ?_⟩
    · have h := congrArg (fun g : realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian ↦
        ((g : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7) : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7))) hpq
      simp only [f, hF] at h
      have := (monomialGroupEquiv hb hQ).injective (a₁ := (p.1, p.2)) (a₂ := (q.1, q.2))
        (Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by
          rw [coe_monomialGroupEquiv_apply, coe_monomialGroupEquiv_apply]
          exact h)))
      rw [Prod.mk.injEq] at this
      exact Prod.ext (Subtype.ext this.1) this.2
    · obtain ⟨s, hs, hgs | hgs⟩ := mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_iff.mp g.property
      · exact ⟨(⟨s, hs⟩, 1), Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext (by rw [hF, hgs]; simp))⟩
      · exact ⟨(⟨s, hs⟩, -1), Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext (by rw [hF, hgs]; simp))⟩
  rw [← Nat.card_congr (Equiv.ofBijective f hbij), Nat.card_prod, Nat.card_eq_fintype_card,
    Fintype.card_coe, card_spinSevenSupports]
  simp

/-- The elementary abelian subgroup is finite. -/
instance finite_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian : Finite realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian :=
  Nat.finite_of_card_ne_zero (by simp)

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup has exponent `2`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem exponent_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian :
    Monoid.exponent realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian = 2 := by
  have hdvd : Monoid.exponent realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian ∣ 2 :=
    Monoid.exponent_dvd_of_forall_pow_eq_one fun g ↦
      Subtype.ext <| by
        rw [pow_two]; exact mul_self_eq_one_of_mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian g.property
  have hne : Monoid.exponent realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian ≠ 1 := by
    rw [Ne, Monoid.exp_eq_one_iff]
    intro h
    have := natCard_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian
    rw [Nat.card_of_subsingleton (1 : realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian)] at this
    omega
  rcases (Nat.dvd_prime Nat.prime_two).mp hdvd with h | h
  · exact absurd h hne
  · exact h

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup is commutative**, as it has exponent `2`. -/
instance realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_isMulCommutative :
    IsMulCommutative realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian :=
  ⟨⟨mul_comm_of_exponent_two exponent_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian⟩⟩

/-! ### The centralizer -/

/-- The coordinates are told apart by the three generating supports: the patterns of membership of
the seven indices in `{0, 1, 2, 3}`, `{0, 1, 4, 5}` and `{0, 2, 4, 6}` are the seven nonzero
vectors of `𝔽₂³`. -/
private theorem exists_generator_not_mem_iff : ∀ i j : Fin (0 + 7), i ≠ j →
    ∃ s ∈ spinSevenSupports, ¬(i ∈ s ↔ j ∈ s) := by
  decide

/-- An even support whose basis monomial commutes with the basis monomials of the eight supports is
itself one of them. The parities compared are the signs of `e_s * e_t` and `e_t * e_s` in
`CliffordAlgebra.basis_mul_basis`. -/
private theorem mem_spinSevenSupports_of_parity : ∀ t : Finset (Fin (0 + 7)), Even t.card →
    (∀ s ∈ spinSevenSupports,
      (∑ i ∈ s, (t.filter (· < i)).card) % 2 = (∑ i ∈ t, (s.filter (· < i)).card) % 2) →
    t ∈ spinSevenSupports := by
  decide +kernel

/-- The basis monomial of a support is an element of the elementary abelian subgroup. -/
private theorem spinBasis_mem {s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))} (hs : s ∈ spinSevenSupports) :
    spinBasis s (even_card_of_mem_spinSevenSupports hs) ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian :=
  mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_iff.mpr ⟨s, hs, Or.inl (coe_spinBasis _ _)⟩

/-- The basis monomial `e_s` of an even support negates the coordinates in `s`. -/
private theorem spinVectorAction_spinBasis_apply (s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) (hs : Even s.card)
    (w : Fin (0 + 7) → ℝ) (j : Fin (0 + 7)) :
    spinVectorAction _ (spinBasis s hs) w j = (if j ∈ s then -1 else 1) * w j := by
  simpa only [Pi.basisFun_repr] using basis_repr_spinVectorAction_of_coe_eq
    (isOrthoᵢ_associated_realCliffordForm 0 7) hs (g := spinBasis s hs)
    (Or.inl (coe_spinBasis s hs)) w j

/-- The basis monomial `e_s` of an even support negates the coordinate vectors indexed by `s` and
fixes the others. -/
private theorem spinVectorAction_spinBasis_single (s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) (hs : Even s.card)
    (i : Fin (0 + 7)) :
    spinVectorAction _ (spinBasis s hs) (Pi.single i 1) =
      if i ∈ s then -Pi.single i 1 else Pi.single i 1 := by
  have h := spinVectorAction_basis_of_coe_eq (isOrthoᵢ_associated_realCliffordForm 0 7) hs
    (g := spinBasis s hs) (Or.inl (coe_spinBasis s hs)) i
  rw [Pi.basisFun_apply] at h
  rw [h]
  split_ifs <;> simp

/-- The Spin action of `e_s` as the diagonal matrix of signs, `-1` on the indices in `s`. -/
private theorem toLinearMap_spinVectorAction_spinBasis (s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7)))
    (hs : Even s.card) :
    (spinVectorAction _ (spinBasis s hs)).toLinearMap =
      Matrix.toLin' (Matrix.diagonal fun i ↦ if i ∈ s then -1 else 1) := by
  refine (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))).ext fun i ↦ ?_
  simp only [Pi.basisFun_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, Matrix.toLin'_apply,
    Matrix.diagonal_mulVec_single, mul_one, spinVectorAction_spinBasis_single]
  split_ifs <;> simp [Pi.single_neg]

/-- The coordinates negated by the Spin action of `x`: the indices `i` with `x • eᵢ = -eᵢ`. -/
private noncomputable def negSupport (x : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7) : Finset (Fin (0 + 7)) :=
  Finset.univ.filter fun i ↦ spinVectorAction _ x (Pi.single i 1) = -Pi.single i 1

/-- An element of the centralizer of the elementary abelian subgroup sends every coordinate vector
`eᵢ` to `±eᵢ`. Its image of `eᵢ` lies in the same eigenspaces of the three diagonal sign changes
`e_s` as `eᵢ` does, and these joint eigenspaces are the coordinate lines. -/
private theorem spinVectorAction_single_eq_or {x : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7}
    (hx : x ∈ Subgroup.centralizer (realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian : Set _))
    (i : Fin (0 + 7)) :
    spinVectorAction _ x (Pi.single i 1) = Pi.single i 1 ∨
      spinVectorAction _ x (Pi.single i 1) = -Pi.single i 1 := by
  set v := spinVectorAction _ x (Pi.single i 1) with hv
  -- `x` commutes with `e_s`, so `e_s` scales `v` by its eigenvalue on `eᵢ`.
  have heig (s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) (hs : s ∈ spinSevenSupports) (j : Fin (0 + 7)) :
      (if j ∈ s then -1 else 1) * v j = (if i ∈ s then -1 else 1) * v j := by
    have hcomm := congrArg (fun g ↦ spinVectorAction _ g (Pi.single i 1))
      ((Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mp hx) _ (spinBasis_mem hs))
    simp only [spinVectorAction_mul, mul_apply_eq_comp, spinVectorAction_spinBasis_single,
      apply_ite (spinVectorAction _ x), map_neg, ← hv] at hcomm
    rw [← spinVectorAction_spinBasis_apply s (even_card_of_mem_spinSevenSupports hs) v j, hcomm]
    split_ifs <;> simp
  have hvj (j : Fin (0 + 7)) (hji : j ≠ i) : v j = 0 := by
    obtain ⟨s, hs, hne⟩ := exists_generator_not_mem_iff i j (Ne.symm hji)
    have := heig s hs j
    split_ifs at this <;> grind
  have hsingle : v = (v i) • Pi.single i 1 := by
    funext j
    by_cases hji : j = i
    · subst hji
      simp
    · simp [hvj j hji, hji]
  -- The action preserves the quadratic form, so `v i` squares to `1`.
  have hQ := spinVectorAction_map_app (realCliffordForm 0 7) x (Pi.single i 1)
  rw [← hv, hsingle, QuadraticMap.map_smul,
    realCliffordForm_single_one_of_le (Nat.zero_le _), smul_eq_mul] at hQ
  rcases mul_self_eq_one_iff.mp (by linarith : v i * v i = 1) with h | h <;>
    rw [hsingle, h] <;> simp

/-- The Spin action of an element of the centralizer as the diagonal matrix of signs, `-1` on the
indices of `negSupport x`. -/
private theorem toLinearMap_spinVectorAction_eq_toLin' {x : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7}
    (hx : x ∈ Subgroup.centralizer (realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian : Set _)) :
    (spinVectorAction _ x).toLinearMap =
      Matrix.toLin' (Matrix.diagonal fun i ↦ if i ∈ negSupport x then -1 else 1) := by
  refine (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))).ext fun i ↦ ?_
  simp only [Pi.basisFun_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, Matrix.toLin'_apply,
    Matrix.diagonal_mulVec_single, negSupport, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and,
    mul_one]
  rcases spinVectorAction_single_eq_or hx i with h | h <;> split_ifs <;>
    simp_all [Pi.single_neg]

/-- **An element of the centralizer is a signed basis monomial** `±e_t` of an even support `t`.
Its Spin action is the diagonal sign change in the coordinates of `t`, of determinant one, so `t`
is even and `x` has the action of `e_t`; the kernel of the action is `±1`. -/
private theorem exists_isSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven_of_mem_centralizer {x : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7}
    (hx : x ∈ Subgroup.centralizer (realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian : Set _)) :
    ∃ t : Finset (Fin (0 + 7)), Even t.card ∧ IsSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven x t := by
  have hdet := congrArg Units.val (QuadraticMap.det_coe_specialOrthogonalGroup
    (spinToSpecialOrthogonal (realCliffordForm 0 7) x))
  have heven : Even (negSupport x).card := by
    rw [← neg_one_pow_eq_one_iff_even (R := ℝ) (by norm_num)]
    simpa [coe_spinToSpecialOrthogonal, LinearEquiv.coe_det,
      toLinearMap_spinVectorAction_eq_toLin' hx, Matrix.det_diagonal, Finset.prod_ite_mem]
      using hdet
  refine ⟨negSupport x, heven, ?_⟩
  have hρ : spinToSpecialOrthogonal (realCliffordForm 0 7) x =
      spinToSpecialOrthogonal (realCliffordForm 0 7) (spinBasis (negSupport x) heven) :=
    Subtype.ext (LinearEquiv.toLinearMap_injective (by
      rw [coe_spinToSpecialOrthogonal, coe_spinToSpecialOrthogonal,
        toLinearMap_spinVectorAction_eq_toLin' hx, toLinearMap_spinVectorAction_spinBasis]))
  rcases eq_or_eq_negOne_mul_of_spinToSpecialOrthogonal_eq _ (nondegenerate_realCliffordForm 0 7)
    x _ hρ with h | h
  · exact Or.inl ((congrArg Subtype.val h).trans (coe_spinBasis _ heven))
  · exact Or.inr (by rw [congrArg Subtype.val h]; simp)

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup is its own centralizer** in the Spin group of
`realCliffordForm 0 7`. An element `x` commuting with it acts on `ℝ⁷` preserving the joint
eigenspaces of the three sign changes `e₀e₁e₂e₃`, `e₀e₁e₄e₅`, `e₀e₂e₄e₆`, which are the seven
coordinate lines. So `x = ±e_t` for an even support `t`, and `e_t` commutes with the three
generators exactly when `t` is one of the eight supports. -/
theorem centralizer_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian :
    Subgroup.centralizer (realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian : Set (realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7)) =
      realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun x hx ↦ ?_)
    (Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff_isMulCommutative.mpr inferInstance)
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hxt⟩ := exists_isSignedBasisSpinZeroSeven_of_mem_centralizer hx
  have hcomm (s : Finset (Fin (0 + 7))) (hs : s ∈ spinSevenSupports) :
      basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s *
          basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) t =
        basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) t *
          basis (realCliffordForm 0 7) (Pi.basisFun ℝ (Fin (0 + 7))) s := by
    have h := congrArg (fun g : realCliffordSpinGroup 0 7 ↦
      (g : CliffordAlgebra (realCliffordForm 0 7)))
      ((Subgroup.mem_centralizer_iff.mp hx) _ (spinBasis_mem hs))
    simp only [Submonoid.coe_mul, coe_spinBasis] at h
    rcases hxt with hxt | hxt <;> rw [hxt] at h
    · exact h
    · simpa only [mul_neg, neg_mul, neg_inj] using h
  refine mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian_iff.mpr
    ⟨t, mem_spinSevenSupports_of_parity t ht fun s hs ↦
      (commute_basis_iff (isOrthoᵢ_associated_realCliffordForm 0 7) (fun i ↦ by
        simp [realCliffordForm_single_one_of_le (Nat.zero_le _)]) s t).mp (hcomm s hs), hxt⟩

/-! ### The compact Spin group -/

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup of order `16` in the compact Spin group** `Spin(7)`, the
Spin group of the positive-definite form `realCliffordForm 7 0`: the image of
`TauCeti.realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian` under the isomorphism
`CliffordAlgebra.realCliffordSpinGroupEquivNeg 0 7`. -/
noncomputable def realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian : Subgroup (realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0) :=
  realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian.map (realCliffordSpinGroupEquivNeg 0 7).toMonoidHom

/-- The defining equation of the elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)`. -/
theorem realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_def : realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian =
    realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian.map (realCliffordSpinGroupEquivNeg 0 7).toMonoidHom :=
  (rfl)

/-- Membership in the elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)`: the preimage under
`CliffordAlgebra.realCliffordSpinGroupEquivNeg 0 7` lies in
`TauCeti.realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian`. -/
theorem mem_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_iff {g : realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0} :
    g ∈ realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian ↔
      (realCliffordSpinGroupEquivNeg 0 7).symm g ∈ realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian :=
  Subgroup.mem_map_equiv

/-- Every element of the elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)` squares to `1`. -/
theorem mul_self_eq_one_of_mem_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian {g : realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0}
    (hg : g ∈ realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian) : g * g = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨h, hh, rfl⟩ := Subgroup.mem_map.mp hg
  rw [← map_mul, mul_self_eq_one_of_mem_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian hh, map_one]

/-- The elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)` is commutative. -/
instance realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_isMulCommutative :
    IsMulCommutative realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian :=
  Subgroup.map_isMulCommutative _ _

/-- The elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)` has order `16`. -/
@[simp]
theorem natCard_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian : Nat.card realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian = 16 := by
  rw [realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian,
    Subgroup.card_map_of_injective (realCliffordSpinGroupEquivNeg 0 7).injective,
    natCard_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian]

/-- The elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)` is finite. -/
instance finite_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian : Finite realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian :=
  Nat.finite_of_card_ne_zero (by simp)

/-- The elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)` has exponent `2`. -/
@[simp]
theorem exponent_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian :
    Monoid.exponent realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian = 2 := by
  rw [realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian, ← Monoid.exponent_eq_of_mulEquiv
    (realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian.equivMapOfInjective _
      (realCliffordSpinGroupEquivNeg 0 7).injective),
    exponent_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian]

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)` is its own centralizer**, by
`TauCeti.centralizer_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian` and the isomorphism
`CliffordAlgebra.realCliffordSpinGroupEquivNeg 0 7`. -/
theorem centralizer_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian :
    Subgroup.centralizer (realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian : Set (realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0)) =
      realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian := by
  rw [realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian, Subgroup.coe_map, MulEquiv.coe_toMonoidHom,
    MulEquiv.toMonoidHom_eq_coe, ← MulEquiv.map_centralizer,
    centralizer_realSpinZeroSevenElementaryAbelian]

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)` is a maximal commutative subgroup**: every
commutative subgroup containing it is equal to it, since such a subgroup lies in the centralizer.
So it is a finite maximal abelian subgroup of the compact connected group `Spin(7)`. -/
theorem eq_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_of_le {H : Subgroup (realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0)}
    [IsMulCommutative H] (hH : realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian ≤ H) :
    H = realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ hH
  calc H ≤ Subgroup.centralizer (H : Set (realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0)) :=
        Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff_isMulCommutative.mpr inferInstance
    _ ≤ Subgroup.centralizer (realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian : Set _) :=
        Subgroup.centralizer_le hH
    _ = realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian := centralizer_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup of `Spin(7)` lies in the image of no homomorphism from a
commutative group in which every element is a square.** Such an image is commutative, so if it
contained the subgroup it would equal it (`TauCeti.eq_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_of_le`).
Every element of the image would then be the square of an element of the subgroup, hence `1`,
whereas the subgroup has order `16`. -/
theorem not_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_le_range_of_forall_exists_mul_self_eq {A : Type*}
    [CommGroup A] (hA : ∀ a : A, ∃ c, c * c = a) (f : A →* realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0) :
    ¬realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian ≤ f.range := by
  intro hle
  have heq := eq_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_of_le hle
  have hne : realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian ≠ ⊥ := fun h ↦ by
    simpa [h] using natCard_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian
  obtain ⟨⟨g, hg⟩, hg1⟩ := Subgroup.ne_bot_iff_exists_ne_one.mp hne
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hle hg
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hA a
  have hc : f c ∈ realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian := heq ▸ MonoidHom.mem_range.mpr ⟨c, rfl⟩
  exact hg1 (Subtype.ext (by
    simpa using mul_self_eq_one_of_mem_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian hc))

/-- **The elementary abelian subgroup of order `16` of `Spin(7)` lies in no torus**: it is not
contained in the image of any homomorphism from a torus `∀ i, AddCircle (p i)`, of any rank,
because every point of a torus is twice another one. -/
theorem not_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_le_range {ι : Type*} (p : ι → ℝ)
    (f : Multiplicative (∀ i, AddCircle (p i)) →* realCliffordSpinGroup 7 0) :
    ¬realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian ≤ f.range := by
  refine not_realSpinSevenElementaryAbelian_le_range_of_forall_exists_mul_self_eq (fun a ↦ ?_) f
  -- Halve a real lift of each coordinate.
  choose r hr using fun i ↦ QuotientAddGroup.mk_surjective (a.toAdd i)
  refine ⟨Multiplicative.ofAdd fun i ↦ ((r i / 2 : ℝ) : AddCircle (p i)), ?_⟩
  apply Multiplicative.toAdd.injective
  funext i
  rw [toAdd_mul, toAdd_ofAdd, Pi.add_apply, ← AddCircle.coe_add, add_halves, ← hr i]

end TauCeti
